WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.031 --> 00:00:11.583
"It will be easy to find someone to help," Ally thought as she walked through Sandville's downtown area.

2
00:00:11.584 --> 00:00:16.698
But Ally didn't spot any 'Help Wanted' signs. Nor did she pick up any cries for help.

3
00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:23.287
In fact, she saw hardly any humans on the street. Most of them were zooming by in vehicles.

4
00:00:23.288 --> 00:00:28.763
Finally she spotted a man walking a four-legged animal with fluffy fur.

5
00:00:28.764 --> 00:00:38.358
She tried to read the man's thoughts but could pick up only a few words: "Milk . . . bread . . . dog biscuits."

6
00:00:38.359 --> 00:00:44.303
It didn't sound like a cry for help, but Ally hurried toward him anyway.

7
00:00:44.304 --> 00:00:52.415
"Greetings! I am Allyzooba of Astralia. Can I be of help to you?"

8
00:00:52.416 --> 00:00:55.223
The man scooped up his animal and backed away.

9
00:00:55.224 --> 00:01:04.627
Then he hurried off, muttering, "Kids these days are so weird!"

10
00:01:04.628 --> 00:01:12.452
A little farther down the street, a woman stepped out of a store and headed to her vehicle.

11
00:01:12.453 --> 00:01:17.491
Ally tried to read her thoughts, but once again the words and images were fuzzy.

12
00:01:17.492 --> 00:01:23.709
Ally sighed. Finding a human to help was going to be more challenging than she'd first thought.

13
00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:28.658
Especially since her Astral mind abilities weren't working well on this strange planet.

14
00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:34.055
But as she glimpsed her reflection in a large plate-glass window, something occurred to her.

15
00:01:34.056 --> 00:01:36.915
Her new human hair was long and thick.

16
00:01:36.916 --> 00:01:42.927
"Hey!" she thought. "Maybe my hair is creating problems."

17
00:01:42.928 --> 00:01:45.969
She tucked her hair behind her ears and listened again.

18
00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:49.493
This time a voice rang clearly in her head.

19
00:01:49.494 --> 00:01:54.070
"I need help . . . I can't do everything myself."

20
00:01:54.071 --> 00:01:59.097
Ally looked around. The cry was coming from the building right in front of her!

21
00:01:59.098 --> 00:02:05.945
She held up her meld medallion to read the sign on the window: Ray's Diner.

22
00:02:05.946 --> 00:02:13.100
She hurried inside. Unlike Pepe's Diner, this one was almost empty.

23
00:02:13.101 --> 00:02:19.780
Three people in a booth were sipping hot beverages, and a man wearing a blue uniform and badge was sitting at the counter.

24
00:02:19.781 --> 00:02:26.071
"I bet he's the one in charge," Ally thought.

25
00:02:26.072 --> 00:02:30.349
"Greetings! Are you the commander here?" she asked.

26
00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.833
The man looked up and laughed.

27
00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:36.251
"Me? I'm just a museum security guard.

28
00:02:36.252 --> 00:02:44.354
Ray's the one in charge around here." He pointed at a man working inside the kitchen.

29
00:02:44.355 --> 00:02:52.591
Ally walked into the kitchen. "Greetings! I am Allyzooba of Astralia."

30
00:02:52.592 --> 00:03:02.196
But there was so much noise from the grill and fan, the human named Ray didn't even turn around.

31
00:03:02.197 --> 00:03:05.919
"Excuse me." Ally tapped him on the shoulder.

32
00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:15.877
"I am Allyzooba of Astralia. I have come to solve your woes, to do good deeds, and to spread great joy."

33
00:03:15.878 --> 00:03:20.912
"You don't sound like you're from Australia!" Ray shouted over the noise.

34
00:03:20.913 --> 00:03:28.020
"Not Australia—Astralia!" Ally shouted back. "And I have come to do—"

35
00:03:28.021 --> 00:03:33.554
"Look, Ally." Ray wiped his brow. "Is it a job you want?"

36
00:03:33.555 --> 00:03:36.600
She nodded.

37
00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:39.189
"Well, I'll hire you," Ray said.

38
00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:45.122
"I need help because I can't cook, wash dishes, and wait on customers by myself.

39
00:03:45.123 --> 00:03:49.190
My son usually helps me, but he's busy this summer with soccer camp.

40
00:03:49.191 --> 00:03:54.433
And I'll be honest. I can't pay you much. You'll have to work for tips."

41
00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:59.162
"You mean I can help you and get paid—in dollars?"

42
00:03:59.163 --> 00:04:02.899
"It's not a lot, nothing to get excited about."

43
00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:06.788
"Well, I'm really excited!" Ally exclaimed.

44
00:04:06.789 --> 00:04:10.820
Ray smiled and grabbed an apron from a hook on the wall.

45
00:04:10.821 --> 00:04:14.297
He handed it to Ally, and she put it on.

46
00:04:14.298 --> 00:04:23.476
Then he went over to pick up a plate with a triple-decker sandwich. "Here. Take this."

47
00:04:23.477 --> 00:04:26.484
"Thanks!" Ally licked her lips.

48
00:04:26.485 --> 00:04:34.140
She was about to take a bite when Ray shouted, "No! What are you doing? That's for Phil at the counter!"

49
00:04:34.141 --> 00:04:38.421
"Oh! This is for a customer to eat!" Ally realized.

50
00:04:38.422 --> 00:04:41.324
She headed out of the kitchen with the plate.

51
00:04:41.325 --> 00:04:45.814
But on the way out, she tripped. "Whoa!"

52
00:04:45.815 --> 00:04:51.035
The customers gasped as the sandwich slipped back and forth on the plate.

53
00:04:51.036 --> 00:04:57.202
Then, in the nick of time, Ally managed to catch her balance and save the sandwich.

54
00:04:57.203 --> 00:05:03.377
"Hooray!" The customers clapped.

55
00:05:03.378 --> 00:05:07.987
Ally smiled and took an Astralian bow.

56
00:05:07.988 --> 00:05:13.185
"Some earthlings are friendly, just as the computer said," she thought.

57
00:05:13.186 --> 00:05:19.714
But others, like the waitress at Pepe's and the man with the furry animal, had treated her rather meanly.

58
00:05:19.715 --> 00:05:25.298
"No wonder humans also have a reputation for being dangerous," she thought.

59
00:05:25.299 --> 00:05:27.702
"They're so unpredictable!"

60
00:05:27.703 --> 00:05:31.980
Plus, Earthlings had never made contact with an Astralian before.

61
00:05:31.981 --> 00:05:40.912
So while Ally was here on Earth, she would have to be careful—very careful.

